```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}

\begin{document}

Given \( n \) points in the plane. Each point is represented by an ordered pair \( (x, y) \) (the point \( (5, 6) \) is different from the point \( (6, 5) \)). Propose a data structure that supports the following operations:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{Insert(x, y)} – Adds the point \( (x, y) \) to the structure.
    \item \texttt{Delete(x, y)} – Removes the point \( (x, y) \) from the structure if it was present. Otherwise, does nothing.
    \item \texttt{Member(x, y)} – Returns \texttt{True} if the point \( (x, y) \) is in the structure. Otherwise, returns \texttt{False}.
\end{itemize}

The worst-case complexity of all the above operations should be \( O(\log n) \).

\end{document}
```

