\section*{Data Structure Description: Minimum Heap and Hash Table with Mutual Pointers}

The key is the length of the segment.

\subsection*{Implementation of Find-Min Operation and Running Time Analysis}

Return the root of the heap (min operation of the heap).

\subsection*{Implementation of Delete and Insert Operations, and Running Time Analysis}

When inserting, insert into both the heap and the table, and update the table with a pointer to the location in the heap. When deleting, find the key in the hash table, get a pointer based on it, and delete from the heap. Also delete from the table. During insertion or deletion, if the position has changed, update the pointer in the hash table.

\subsection*{Implementation of the Building Process and Running Time Analysis}

Build a binary heap in linear time. Insert each element into the hash table using chaining, at the head of the list, and simultaneously update the pointer to the location in the heap.

\end{document}
```

